    {
      "dom_id": "question-50157",
      "name": null,
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14223512/assets/b45ab87c3b5f6b083ca5828676ca96486e3825b3b3fbbfc3f31d19fa65a215b5.png)\n\nThe diagram shown above is the slope field for which of the following differential equations?",
      "worked_solution": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14223512/assets/ef837c5bdd4198651302e77b70d592c7771071a1ee3543ce76a3685b0439fa82.png)\n\nNotice the following properties of the given slope field:\n\n- First, the slopes of the slope field are horizontal along the lines $x=-1$ and $y=-2,$ as shown above. Therefore, the right-hand side of the differential equation should evaluate to zero on both of these lines. \n\nOf the given equations, the only equations that satisfy this condition are the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =(x+1)(y+2) \\\\ {y}^{′} & =(x+1)^{2}(y+2)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Second, the lines $x=-1$ and $y=-2$ divide the plane into $4$ regions. The sign of the slopes in each of the $4$ regions are easily deduced by considering the behavior of the solution curves in these regions. This information is summarized in the following table:\n\n| $y>-2$ | $↘$\n\n$(-)$ | $↗$\n\n$(+)$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $y<-2$ | $↗$\n\n$(+)$ | $↘$\n\n$(-)$ |\n|  | $x<-1$ | $x>-1$ |\n\nOf the remaining options, the only one that gives this behavior is\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=(x+1)(y+2).\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [],
      "problem_field_keys": [],
      "answer_fields_complete": null,
      "result": "Incorrect",
      "proof_feedback": null,
      "html": "<div id=\"question-50157\" class=\"question\"><div class=\"questionHeader\"><span class=\"questionNumber\">2.</span><a class=\"questionKP\" href=\"/topics/3350#7126\">Identifying an Equation That Generates a Slope Field Using the Sign of the Slopes</a><span class=\"helpButton\" questionid=\"50157\">?</span></div><div class=\"questionGraphicFrame\"><img class=\"questionGraphic\" src=\"/graphics/q-50157\"></div><div class=\"questionText\"><p>The diagram shown above is the slope field for which of the following differential equations?</p>\n</div><div class=\"answerDetails\"><div class=\"questionDifficulty difficultyHard\">H</div><span class=\"answerCreated\">Wed, Oct 14th @ 8:46 PM</span><span class=\"answerDetailsSeparator\">|</span><span class=\"timeElpased\">Elapsed: 0:16</span><span class=\"answerResult\"><span style=\"color: red;\">Incorrect</span></span></div></div>",
